.TH BOUNTYTOOL 1 "2026-11-08" "bountytool 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
bountytool \- end-to-end bug bounty reconnaissance, triage and reporting
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bountytool
[\fITARGET\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.br
.B bountytool
\fBdoctor\fR [\fB\-\-install\fR] [\fB\-\-group\fR \fIGROUP\fR]
.br
.B bountytool
\fBsessions\fR [\fB\-\-limit\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR]
.br
.B bountytool
\fBconfig\fR [\fB\-\-init\fR] [\fB\-\-file\fR \fIFILE\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bountytool
runs an ordered pipeline over an authorised target: scope validation, passive
subdomain enumeration, DNS resolution, HTTP probing, fingerprinting, optional
port scanning, crawling, content and parameter discovery, template scanning,
native vulnerability probes, triage, and a report.
.PP
Two frontends share one engine. Without \fB\-\-tui\fR the tool prints progress
on stderr and a result summary on stdout, which suits scripting. With
\fB\-\-tui\fR it takes over the terminal with a live dashboard.
.PP
Active scanning is refused unless \fB\-y\fR is passed and a scope is declared.
Loopback and RFC1918 targets require \fBallow_private_ips = true\fR in the scope
file.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-p, \-\-profile \fIPROFILE\fR
Scan depth: \fBlight\fR, \fBstandard\fR (default) or \fBdeep\fR. Each profile is
a superset of the previous one.
.TP
.B \-\-scope \fIFILE\fR
Scope file. A \fIscope.toml\fR in the working directory is used automatically.
.TP
.B \-\-in\-scope \fIHOST\fR
Add an in-scope host or domain. Repeatable.
.TP
.B \-y, \-\-i\-have\-authorization
Confirm you are permitted to test the target. Required.
.TP
.B \-\-tui
Run the scan in the full-screen TUI.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Print the external commands the pipeline would run without running them.
.TP
.B \-\-only \fISTAGE\fR
Run only the listed stages. Accepts a comma separated list.
.TP
.B \-\-skip \fISTAGE\fR
Skip the listed stages.
.TP
.B \-f, \-\-format \fIFORMAT\fR
Report formats: \fBmd\fR, \fBjson\fR, \fBhtml\fR. Defaults to all three.
.TP
.B \-\-resume \fIDIR\fR
Continue a previous session, skipping stages that already completed.
.TP
.B \-\-open
Open the HTML report when the scan finishes.
.TP
.B \-\-quiet
Only print the final result.
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-verbose
Include debug logs and raw scanner output.
.SH STAGES
scope, passive, dns, probe, fingerprint, ports, urls, content, params, nuclei,
active, triage, report.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/bountytool/config.toml
User configuration, deep-merged over the compiled defaults.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/bountytool/sessions/
One directory per scan: \fIsession.json\fR manifest, \fIartifacts/\fR, \fIraw/\fR
and the generated reports.
.TP
.I ./scope.toml
Scope used when \fB\-\-scope\fR is not given.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B BOUNTYTOOL_CONCURRENCY, BOUNTYTOOL_RATE_LIMIT, BOUNTYTOOL_PER_HOST_BUDGET
Override the matching configuration keys.
.TP
.B BOUNTYTOOL_SECLISTS, BOUNTYTOOL_WORDLIST
Wordlist locations.
.TP
.B BOUNTYTOOL_OUTPUT
Session output root.
.TP
.B BOUNTYTOOL_OAST, BOUNTYTOOL_SQLMAP
Enable out-of-band callbacks or sqlmap confirmation.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Generic failure.
.TP
.B 2
A required external tool is missing.
.TP
.B 3
Scope or authorization refusal.
.TP
.B 4
Configuration error.
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
bountytool example.com \-y
bountytool example.com \-y \-\-tui
bountytool example.com \-y \-\-profile deep \-f html \-\-open
bountytool example.com \-y \-\-only probe,nuclei,active,report
bountytool doctor \-\-install \-\-group recommended
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nmap (1),
.BR ffuf (1),
.BR nuclei (1),
.BR sqlmap (1)
